            "jsdoc": {
              "purpose": "Loads the signed-in person's own access state in one call: their record, whether access is complete, what is missing and the privacy text to accept when consent is required.",
              "input": "None. The person is the signed-in login, resolved by the server.",
              "processing": "Resolves the single person record linked to the signed-in login through the platform session resolver (oneMemberPerLogin); never creates or links another record. Computes accessComplete with the same platform completeness rule the session uses (accessCompleteByPlatformRule) and missingItems among name, country and privacy consent (only when the country is Brazil or an EU country), plus an unlinked login stated as resolved by the owner through the platform access release (pendingItemHasActionOrResolver). consentRequired is true only when the country requires consent and no valid consent is recorded (validConsentNotAskedAgain). The country is returned as stored, never defaulted (countryNeverDefaulted). loginEmail is the authenticated account e-mail, read-only, never from contact data (loginEmailReadOnly). Returns the current identified privacy text and version (consentExplicitUnchecked). Derived fields are computed, never stored.",
              "output": "The person's record with id, version, name, status, country, recorded consent, accessComplete, missingItems, loginEmail and consentRequired, plus the privacy text and version."
