            "jsdoc": {
              "purpose": "Saves the missing name, country and privacy consent on the signed-in person's own record and returns it as really saved.",
              "input": "id and version of the person's record (optimistic concurrency); name and countryCode only when they were missing; privacyConsent with the textId and textVersion that were shown, only when explicitly accepted.",
              "processing": "Refuses a record other than the one linked to the signed-in login (oneMemberPerLogin). Saves only name, country and consent through entity.update; a missing country is refused, never defaulted (countryNeverDefaulted). Records the consent only from an explicit acceptance, never implied by a country change (consentExplicitUnchecked), with date, time and channel set by the server and the version shown; an empty, invalid or revoked consent does not complete access (consentRecordedByServer). A valid recorded consent is kept and not overwritten (validConsentNotAskedAgain). Grants no role or permission (dataEntryGrantsNoRole). After saving, reads the record again by id and refreshes the platform session so accessComplete matches the session (accessCompleteByPlatformRule); accessComplete and missingItems are computed, never stored.",
